{
  "title": "{ip:Va} detto che si {pp:è fatto} il possibile",
  "translation": "It must be said that everything possible was done",
  "topics": "Choosing among passive and impersonal forms according to focus and style",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "One event, many focuses"
      },
      "Each form answers a slightly different need. Choosing well means deciding what should be foregrounded and who should stay in the dark.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Active",
              "Il governo {pp:ha ridotto} le tasse.",
              "names who is responsible"
            ],
            [
              "Passive with essere",
              "Le tasse {pp:sono state} {pp:ridotte} dal governo.",
              "foregrounds the tax"
            ],
            [
              "Passive without agent",
              "Le tasse {pp:sono state} {pp:ridotte}.",
              "hides who did it"
            ],
            [
              "Passive si",
              "Si {pp:sono ridotte} le tasse.",
              "general, impersonal"
            ],
            [
              "venire",
              "Le tasse {ip:vengono} ridotte ogni anno.",
              "shows a process"
            ],
            [
              "andare",
              "Le tasse {ip:vanno} ridotte.",
              "says it's necessary"
            ],
            [
              "Third person plural",
              "{pp:Hanno ridotto} le tasse.",
              "«they», informal"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Who is hiding behind the passive?"
      },
      "*{pp:Sono stati} {pp:commessi} errori* admits a fault without saying whose. Being able to spot this is as useful as being able to write it, and the phrase is typical of institutional language.",
      {
        "h": "Ways of saying «people»"
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Form",
            "Example",
            "Register"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "si",
              "Si {ip:dice} che {csp:sia} vero.",
              "neutral"
            ],
            [
              "uno",
              "Uno non {ip:sa} mai che fare.",
              "colloquial, personal"
            ],
            [
              "tu generic",
              "{ip:Lavori} tutta la vita e poi…",
              "colloquial, involving"
            ],
            [
              "noi",
              "Come {pp:abbiamo visto}, …",
              "academic, inclusive"
            ],
            [
              "loro",
              "{ip:Dicono} che {csp:sia} vero.",
              "conversational"
            ],
            [
              "la gente",
              "La gente {ip:pensa} che…",
              "conversational"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "Keeping si under control"
      },
      "With a reflexive verb, the sequence becomes *ci si*: *Ci si abitua a tutto*. With a pronoun, *lo* comes first: *Lo si {ip:vede} subito*. And *ne* gives *se ne {ip:parla}*. Don't stack too many impersonal forms, or the reader will lose track of the subject.",
      {
        "h": "Fixed expressions"
      },
      "*{ip:Viene} da pensare* (one is led to think), *{ip:va} detto che* (it must be said), *{ip:va} da sé* (it goes without saying), *si {ip:fa} per dire* (so to speak), *si salvi chi {ip:può}* (every man for himself)."
    ]
  },
